OneiOS take18, userland/metal/patches/metal2vulkan/0004: an identity texture swizzle skips the border and channel work.
Upstream: Droid-VM/macOS-DroidVM 3d247c4 (lateautumn233, 2026-11-13: patches/metal2vulkan-macos/0005), as Droid-VM/UniXNU
wip/hackintosh patches/metal2vulkan/0042-identity-texture-swizzle.patch; applies here with a 9-line offset.
What: with_border() and reads_unswizzled() answer at once for the default (identity) swizzle instead of deriving the texel
class's borders and channel presence again.
Why: CPU per texture and per bind (macOS-DroidVM: 12 texel-format and 17 heap release checks pass; its Weather CPU
comparisons "vary with workload": a small saving, not a measured fix).
Switch: none (the same answers). Removable: yes (ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=identity-texture-swizzle).

diff --git a/crates/metal2vulkan/src/metal/texel_format.rs b/crates/metal2vulkan/src/metal/texel_format.rs
index 0d4890e..dc61208 100644
--- a/crates/metal2vulkan/src/metal/texel_format.rs
+++ b/crates/metal2vulkan/src/metal/texel_format.rs
@@ -641,7 +641,7 @@ fn two_plane_family(pf: PixelFormat, field: Option<PackedTexels>) -> u32 {
 /// specialization).
 pub fn with_border(pf: PixelFormat, swizzle: TextureSwizzleChannels) -> TexelFormat {
     match texel_format(pf) {
-        class if !class.has_channels() => class,
+        class if !class.has_channels() || swizzle.is_default() => class,
         class => TexelFormat(BicubicTexels(class.0).with_border(pf, swizzle).0),
     }
 }
@@ -664,6 +664,9 @@ pub fn heap_class(pf: PixelFormat, swizzle: TextureSwizzleChannels) -> TexelForm
 /// format's), which keeps the format's class: its field and family.
 pub fn reads_unswizzled(pf: PixelFormat, swizzle: TextureSwizzleChannels) -> bool {
     use crate::metal::TextureSwizzle as S;
+    if swizzle.is_default() {
+        return true;
+    }
     // The class's channels where it states them (a two-plane format's, whatever this crate
     // holds of it), else the format's.
     let class = BicubicTexels(texel_format(pf).0);
